                <pb facs="0170" n="85" sameAs="frus:frus1919v02/pg85"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">123C853/1a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Commission to
                        Negotiate Peace</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-04-18T17:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 18, 1919,
                                5 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>1630. For Lansing: Please convey to the President my sincere appreciation of the
                    honor he has conferred in tendering me the appointment as Minister to
                    Czecho-Slovak Republic and inform the President that I accept. It will be
                    difficult for me to arrange my affairs in less than ten days. Whatever
                    qualifications I have for this post have been developed by my association with
                    you and your confidence in my ability has materially helped me in coming to a
                    decision. Crane.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
